            <h2>What We Need From You</h2>

            <div class="gold-line"></div>

        </div>

        <div class="service-grid">

            <div class="service-card">
                <h3>Book Information</h3>
                <p>
                    Book title, subtitle, author name, genre and
                    a clear description of the book.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="service-card">
                <h3>Book Listing</h3>
                <p>
                    Your existing Amazon book listing link,
                    if the book has already been published.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="service-card">
                <h3>Target Audience</h3>
                <p>
                    Information about the readers you want
                    the book to reach.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="service-card">
                <h3>Book Cover</h3>
                <p>
                    A copy of your approved book cover or
                    relevant design assets.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="service-card">
                <h3>Publishing Details</h3>
                <p>
                    Relevant publishing platform, marketplace
                    and book format information.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="service-card">
                <h3>Creative Direction</h3>
                <p>
                    Your preferences, reference examples and
                    any specific listing requirements.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="notice">
            Do not send your Amazon password or other sensitive
            account credentials through the order form. Any
            account-related work must use an approved and secure
            access method.
        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- PROCESS -->
    <section class="section">

        <div class="section-heading">

            <span class="eyebrow">Our Workflow</span>

            <h2>How the Process Works</h2>

            <div class="gold-line"></div>

        </div>

        <div class="service-grid">

            <div class="service-card">
                <div class="process-number">01</div>
                <h3>Submit Your Request</h3>
                <p>
                    Tell WMF about your book and the optimization
                    support you require.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="service-card">
                <div class="process-number">02</div>
                <h3>Project Review</h3>
                <p>
                    WMF reviews your listing, requirements and
                    requested deliverables.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="service-card">
                <div class="process-number">03</div>
                <h3>Scope Confirmation</h3>
                <p>
                    The exact work, price, schedule and revision
                    terms are confirmed with you.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="service-card">
                <div class="process-number">04</div>
                <h3>Payment</h3>
                <p>
                    Production begins after approval and verification
                    of the required upfront payment.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="service-card">
                <div class="process-number">05</div>
                <h3>Optimization Work</h3>
                <p>
                    WMF completes the agreed research, metadata
                    support and design deliverables.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="service-card">
                <div class="process-number">06</div>
                <h3>Review and Delivery</h3>
                <p>
                    You review the work, request included revisions
                    and receive the approved final deliverables.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="section faq-section">

        <div class="section-heading">

            <span class="eyebrow">Questions and Answers</span>

            <h2>Amazon Optimization FAQs</h2>

            <div class="gold-line"></div>

        </div>

        <div id="amazonFaqs">

            <div class="faq-item">

                <button class="faq-question">
                    What is Amazon book optimization?
                    <span>+</span>
                </button>

                <div class="faq-answer">
                    It involves improving the information and
                    presentation of a book listing through relevant
                    metadata support, keyword research and other
                    agreed listing improvements.
                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">

                <button class="faq-question">
                    What is A+ Content?
                    <span>+</span>
                </button>

                <div class="faq-answer">
                    A+ Content is enhanced product-page content
                    available to eligible publishers and sellers.
                    It can include designed images and other
                    enhanced presentation elements.
                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">

                <button class="faq-question">
                    Is A+ Content available for every author?
                    <span>+</span>
                </button>

                <div class="faq-answer">
                    No. Availability depends on Amazon's current
                    eligibility requirements and the author's
                    publishing or account arrangement.
                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">

                <button class="faq-question">
                    Will optimization guarantee more book sales?
                    <span>+</span>
                </button>

                <div class="faq-answer">
                    No. Optimization can support the quality and
                    discoverability of a listing, but sales,
                    rankings and reader response cannot be guaranteed.
                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">

                <button class="faq-question">
                    Do I need to provide my Amazon password?
                    <span>+</span>
                </button>

                <div class="faq-answer">
                    No. Never submit your password through the
                    website order form. Any account-related work
                    must follow an approved secure access process.
                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">

                <button class="faq-question">
                    How long will the service take?
                    <span>+</span>
                </button>

                <div class="faq-answer">
                    The estimated delivery time depends on the
                    selected scope and project requirements.
                    WMF will confirm the schedule before payment.
                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


